    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0386" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857H.01/104</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d291-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1025</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Riga</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-30">December 30,
                        1935</date>.<lb/>[Received January 14, 1936.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Collection of Laws and Orders of the U.S.S.R.</hi>, in
                    its No. 17, Part II, of November 29, 1935, contains as item 138, the Treaty
                    Concerning the Archipelago of Spitsbergen, together with additions and an annex,
                    signed at Paris, February 9, 1920, with a note that the adhesion of the U.S.S.R.
                    to this Treaty was approved by the Central Executive Committee of the U.S.S.R.
                    February 27, 1935, and came into effect May 7, 1935.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        J. V. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d291-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d291-f1-content">
                <p>Similar information was sent to the Department by the Chargé in the Soviet Union
                    in his despatch No. 1232, January 2, 1936; received January 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
